{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nGate snapshots written by the on-box MCP container land on the container's own writable layer at `/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots` instead of the dedicated gate-scratch EBS volume. `rebar-mcp-4f12815e9a0b-8092` holds 1,341,684,890 B of writable layer, dominated by that directory (3,465,011,200 B by `du`, largest single entry a 1,595,334,656 B tickets-store snapshot). This drove `rebar-container-writable-usage-high` to ALARM at 90.3% of the configured 2 GiB share ceiling.\n\nRoot-cause evidence is in the investigation comment on this ticket.\n\n## Cause\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:mcp_run_new` creates blue-green MCP containers with `docker run` and mirrors many compose settings, but omits **four** that `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` sets:\n\n- `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` — the content-addressed snapshot store's base directory, read by `rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.peek_store_root`.\n- `TMPDIR` — the system temp dir, followed by `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory`. Compose documents these as two distinct consumers and warns that setting only one \"leaves half the bytes on root\".\n- `REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT` — the snapshot janitor's volume-relative reclaim trigger. Without it the janitor falls back to a disk-size-blind absolute threshold, which is why the janitor is running yet bounding nothing.\n- The `-v /var/lib/rebar:/var/lib/rebar` bind that makes the scratch volume reachable at all.\n\nThe scratch volume itself is healthy and 5% used. It is simply not mounted into this container.\n\nThis is a **known defect fixed in one path only**. `docker-compose.yml:258-262` describes this exact failure in the past tense — the store \"sat on the container's writable layer on the ROOT volume because `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` was unset. It is set now.\" That fix, from ADR 0112 decision 3 and story `aa40-cbda-ee38-481c`, was never carried into the autodeploy `docker run` path.\n\n## Why the ADR 0112 guard did not catch it\n\nADR 0112 forbids silent fallback to root, and gate admission decides whether the volume is mounted from a declaration marker on the root filesystem beside the mount point plus a proof marker inside it. Compose binds the **parent** `/var/lib/rebar` rather than the mount point precisely so both markers are visible.\n\nWith no bind at all, the container sees neither marker, so the guard cannot distinguish \"unmounted\" from \"not configured\" and never fires. The guard is structurally blind to this case. The fix must therefore be the parity, not a new guard.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd the four missing settings to `mcp_run_new`, single-sourced against the same values compose uses, and extend the existing parity test so the two paths cannot drift again.\n\n`tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py` already pins agreement between `docker-compose.yml`, terraform's `gate_scratch_mount`, and `observability.sh`'s `GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT`. `autodeploy.sh` is the one participant it does not cover, which is exactly why this drifted. Extending that test is the fix for the class; adding the env vars alone only fixes the instance.\n\nTest first: the added assertions must fail against the current `autodeploy.sh` before the fix is applied, demonstrating they detect the real defect rather than passing vacuously.\n\nRolling the MCP backend to pick up the corrected run path is an operational follow-on, performed after this lands, and is not part of this change.\n\n## Severity note\n\nThis is **not** an imminent outage, contrary to the original filing, which compared it to bug `3276`. The percentage is measured against a configured share ceiling that `container_quota_enforceable = 0` means the host cannot enforce, so crossing 100% alarms and nothing more. Root has roughly 40 GB free. The defect is real and the fix is small, but the deadline is not hours.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Enabling overlay2 quota enforcement. It needs host filesystem support and a reboot, and would not correct the wrong scratch target.\n- Recreating or restarting the running container. A restart does not reclaim the layer, and recreation without this fix merely restarts accumulation.\n- Reducing tickets-store size, which scales every snapshot. Tracked by `3394`.\n- Any change to the exited-container reaper, which is working correctly and has nothing to reclaim.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:mcp_run_new` passes `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` set to the same mount path compose uses. Verified by `grep -q 'REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR' infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `mcp_run_new` passes `TMPDIR` set to that same mount path. Verified by `grep -q 'e TMPDIR=' infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `mcp_run_new` passes `REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT` matching the compose value. Verified by `grep -q 'REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT' infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `mcp_run_new` binds the scratch volume at the parent path `/var/lib/rebar`, not at the mount point, so both ADR 0112 markers are visible. Verified by `grep -q '/var/lib/rebar:/var/lib/rebar' infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py` asserts that `autodeploy.sh`'s MCP run path carries each of those four settings with values matching `docker-compose.yml`. Verified by reading the added assertions and confirming each names `autodeploy`.\n- [ ] Those new assertions fail against the pre-fix `autodeploy.sh`. Verified by stashing the `autodeploy.sh` change, running `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`, and recording a non-zero failure count in a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py` reports 0 failures with the fix applied. Verified by the pytest summary line.\n- [ ] `bash -n infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` exits 0, confirming the edited script still parses. Verified by the exit code.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. Verified by both exiting 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789695967578894971,"uuid":"b6a99faa-d688-4ff5-a95a-360d3c76bfac"}